                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c228158-8ab4-3e27-b405-bd95bf66caca",
                        "entry_id": "12682eb1-dc55-3b8e-9009-64d797d8f150",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Politique ou pratiques de Vladimir Poutine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1b7b73a-d3f8-4cbb-b507-e1302e6d7c94",
                                "sense_id": "2c228158-8ab4-3e27-b405-bd95bf66caca",
                                "text": "Le poutinisme, si tant est qu’il s’agisse d’un courant politique, est une réponse aux défis concrets que la Russie a dû relever au tournant de ce siècle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9eacb299-b929-47b7-82ab-ee53a04e2903",
                                "sense_id": "2c228158-8ab4-3e27-b405-bd95bf66caca",
                                "text": "Demander à ceux qui étudient la Russie depuis des décennies « Qu'est-ce que le poutinisme ? » aboutit rarement à une réponse claire, et elle n'est jamais la même. Qu'est-ce que le poutinisme en effet, sinon l'adhésion à Vladimir Poutine ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "098a3327-a2f5-46c9-88f2-4c4eb3473250",
                        "source_entry_id": "12682eb1-dc55-3b8e-9009-64d797d8f150",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c228158-8ab4-3e27-b405-bd95bf66caca",
                        "target_lang_word": "Putinismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f33e6dfd-3412-48e8-8945-53c3ec7b34da",
                        "source_entry_id": "12682eb1-dc55-3b8e-9009-64d797d8f150",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c228158-8ab4-3e27-b405-bd95bf66caca",
                        "target_lang_word": "Putinism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Putinism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c68c81a4-fdaa-398b-9b02-b103246fd910",
                                        "entry_id": "ac98c73c-1cf2-306e-b1cf-ea69d6dbf2c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The political policies of Vladimir Putin; the Russian political system during Putin’s tenure in power."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "342c67e4-dcbe-44e0-9cf0-574a14e5ff1f",
                                                "sense_id": "c68c81a4-fdaa-398b-9b02-b103246fd910",
                                                "text": "Indeed Putinism elided the differences between consensus, centrism and conformity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0f97155-7646-4782-9e34-6b466a99e58b",
                                                "sense_id": "c68c81a4-fdaa-398b-9b02-b103246fd910",
                                                "text": "Putin may now calculate he can call off the dogs of war, having achieved his aims and able to pocket his gains very cheaply. The Georgia campaign becomes the triumphant climax of Putinism. http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2008/aug/16/georgia.russia1"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4a00f06-c22e-4b07-832e-4cffbd0e22af",
                                                "sense_id": "c68c81a4-fdaa-398b-9b02-b103246fd910",
                                                "text": "And so it was Surkov who in 2004 announced that Putinism, this strange new hybrid of Soviet-type authoritarianism and free-market morals, was based on the concept of ‘sovereign democracy’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "487dce96-85fe-48e4-a0b9-cb578a9264ff",
                                                "sense_id": "c68c81a4-fdaa-398b-9b02-b103246fd910",
                                                "text": "Navalny’s boyish charm, quick wit and detailed accounts of the dodgy deals and luxurious homes of the elite have made his Internet-distributed videos oopular as devastating indictments of the open-mawed corruption of late Putinism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
